#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/vision/optics/field-of-view.rst:97
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"All three columns go through the same formula. The diagonal FOV uses "
":math:`S` equal to the sensor diagonal :math:`\\sqrt{W^2 + H^2}` (6 mm for "
"this sensor); the horizontal FOV uses :math:`S = W = 4.8` mm; the vertical "
"FOV uses :math:`S = H = 3.6` mm. Halving the focal length nearly doubles "
"each cone; doubling it nearly halves them."
msgstr ""
"三個欄位都套用同一個公式。對角線 FOV 使用的 :math:`S` 等於 sensor 對角線 :math:`\\sqrt{W^2 + H^2}`\\"
" （這塊 sensor 為 6 mm）；水平 FOV 使用 :math:`S = W = 4.8` mm；垂直 FOV 使用 :math:`S = H "
"= 3.6` mm。將焦距減半會使每個錐形幾乎加倍；將焦距加倍則會使其幾乎減半。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/vision/optics/field-of-view.rst:104
msgid ""
"Lens datasheets usually publish the *diagonal* FOV as the single headline "
"number, since it spans the sensor corner to corner. The horizontal and "
"vertical FOVs are more directly useful when planning what will fit in the "
"frame, because the frame is rectangular and a rectangular working area is "
"bounded along the horizontal and vertical, not the diagonal."
msgstr ""
"鏡頭資料表通常會將\\ *對角線* FOV 作為唯一的標頭數字公布，因為它涵蓋了 sensor 的對角兩端。在規劃哪些東西能容納進影格時，水平與垂直 "
"FOV 更為直接實用，因為影格是矩形的，而矩形的工作區域是沿著水平與垂直方向受限，而非沿著對角線。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/vision/optics/field-of-view.rst:113
msgid "Choosing a focal length"
msgstr "選擇焦距"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/vision/optics/field-of-view.rst:115
msgid ""
"The FOV the application needs is set by how big a region the camera has to "
"see and how far away the camera will be. If the camera sits 1 m above a 0.6 "
"m × 0.6 m work area, the angular FOV needed to cover one edge is :math:`2 "
"\\cdot \\arctan(0.3 / 1) \\approx 33°`, and the 8 mm lens above comes close."
msgstr ""
"應用所需的 FOV 由相機必須看到多大的區域，以及相機與目標的距離有多遠所決定。如果相機位於一個 0.6 m × 0.6 m 工作區域上方 1 m "
"處，那麼涵蓋其中一邊所需的角度 FOV 為 :math:`2 \\cdot \\arctan(0.3 / 1) \\approx 33°`\\ "
"，而上述的 8 mm 鏡頭相當接近。"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/vision/optics/field-of-view.rst:122
msgid ""
"Going wider than the application needs makes objects smaller in the frame, "
"wastes pixels on background, and increases lens distortion. Going narrower "
"drops parts of the scene off the side of the sensor. The right lens is the "
"longest focal length that still covers the working area at the camera's "
"intended distance."
msgstr ""
"比應用所需更廣會使物體在影格中變小、把像素浪費在背景上，並增加鏡頭畸變。比所需更窄則會使部分場景落到 sensor "
"邊緣之外。最合適的鏡頭，是在相機預定距離下仍能涵蓋工作區域的最長焦距鏡頭。"
